Make CONFIG_ATOMICS opt-out with -DMETACODES_NO_ATOMICS.

Atomics.wait blocks the calling thread and pulls in pthread on every target.
The embedded engine runs one runtime per session thread and never shares a
SharedArrayBuffer across threads, so metacodes builds without Atomics.
Upstream defines CONFIG_ATOMICS unconditionally outside EMSCRIPTEN, so no
compiler flag alone can turn it off.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@
 
 /* define to include Atomics.* operations which depend on the OS
    threads */
-#if !defined(EMSCRIPTEN)
+#if !defined(EMSCRIPTEN) && !defined(METACODES_NO_ATOMICS)
 #define CONFIG_ATOMICS
 #endif
 
